1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,240
TANJRO, LOOK OUT!

2
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:11,200
Damn it!

3
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:15,160
Zenichu, forget about me!

4
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:21,120
This happened because I wasn't paying attention.

5
00:00:22,060 --> 00:00:23,220
I'm sorry, Inosuke.

6
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:26,000
If only I'd noticed him sooner than maybe...

7
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:27,640
No.

8
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:32,900
If I hadn't left Mr. Uzui's side in the first place, this never would have happened.

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:34,660
It's my fault.

10
00:00:36,380 --> 00:00:37,680
I'm sorry, everyone.

11
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,720
Please forgive me.

12
00:00:57,640 --> 00:01:00,660
launches a single point.

13
00:01:00,660 --> 00:01:02,340
is

14
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:05,280
a little too

15
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:35,260
Thank you.

16
00:01:35,280 --> 00:02:05,260
Thank you.

17
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:07,280
Thank you.

18
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,280
Thank you.

19
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:40,280
There's nothing for you to be sorry for.

20
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:45,740
Big brother, why do you always apologize?

21
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:52,700
If we're poor and can't afford to wear nice kimonos, is that something you have to be sorry for?

22
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:56,100
Don't blame yourself for something like that.

23
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:59,680
It would be like blaming father for succumbing to his illness.

24
00:02:59,680 --> 00:03:03,980
He tried as hard as he could, but it wasn't enough.

25
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:05,360
We have to accept that.

26
00:03:05,980 --> 00:03:10,860
We're human after all, and part of that means there are things that are outside of our control.

27
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:18,560
Whether I'm happy or not is up to me, even if it feels like the world is against me.

28
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:24,980
What's most important is that we keep moving forward together, and fight if we must.

29
00:03:24,980 --> 00:03:27,780
So stop apologizing.

30
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:30,760
You of all people should understand.

31
00:03:31,520 --> 00:03:34,420
I want you to understand how I feel.

32
00:03:34,420 --> 00:03:45,520
Was that a dream about the past?

33
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:47,620
Hold on.

34
00:03:48,100 --> 00:03:48,860
Where am I?

35
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:50,420
Am I...

36
00:03:50,420 --> 00:04:06,220
This is awful.

37
00:04:06,980 --> 00:04:08,140
How did it come to this?

38
00:04:09,720 --> 00:04:13,060
I just hope the people who lived here were able to escape.

39
00:04:14,660 --> 00:04:15,220
Nezuko!

40
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:20,220
Nezuko...

41
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,260
Thank you, Nezuko.

42
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:26,180
My fault or not, I've got to do what I can do.

43
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:28,080
Well, I'm impressed.

44
00:04:28,360 --> 00:04:30,440
